  "hashAlgorithm": "blake2b-256",
  "body": {
    "summary": "We have determined that this Hard Fork Initiation governance action is constitutional.",
    "rationaleStatement": "Article II, Section 6.3 of the Cardano Constitution states \"\"Hard Fork Initiation\" and \"Parameter Update\" actions shall undergo sufficient technical review and scrutiny as mandated by the Guardrails to ensure that the governance action does not endanger the security, functionality, performance, or long-term sustainability of the Cardano Blockchain.\"\n\nThe governance action with ID “gov_action1lh2x3kjucjkggvwu6l3txggkvmrnhs3flpv8j35lvlcan4gax3xsq3cxfjc” and title “Hard Fork to Protocol Version 11 ('van Rossem' Hard Fork)”, as a Hard Fork Initiation governance action, states that “The submission of this governance action has been recommended by Intersect's Hard Fork Working Group on 2026-06-15 and further endorsed by Intersect's Technical Steering Committee on 2026-06-16.”  It refers to assessments done relating to Functionality, Security, Performance and Sustainability, and complies with the relevant guardrails, being HARDFORK-01 to HARDFORK-08.\n\nWe therefore find this governance action **Constitutional**.",
    "precedentDiscussion": "None",
    "counterargumentDiscussion": "None",
    "conclusion": "As a Hard Fork Initiation, this governance action has undergone sufficient technical review and complies with the relevant guardrails in the Cardano Constitution, so is deemed constitutional.",
    "internalVote": {
      "constitutional": 5,
      "unconstitutional": 0,
      "abstain": 2,
      "didNotVote": 0
    },
    "references": []
  },
